	(text "Hub connector layer (spec sections 1, 3, 3a). J1 = frozen stack connector to the core layer; +3V3 comes from the Pico.\nModule ports A-C: hub column of the wire plan (SCK on TX+, its return on TX-, MOSI on RX+, MISO on RX-, CS on D+, INT on D-, LED data on SBU).\nTPS25810 per port: CHG high, CHG_HI 100k to +5V = 3 A advertised, 3.4 A limit (fit the DNP 0R to GND for 1.5 A / 1.7 A); UFP low = sink attached (DET).\n74LVC125A per port: SCK, MOSI and the MISO return are enabled only while that port's CS is low; the CS output only while DET is low,\nso an empty or unpowered port, or a phone that never answers, sees no SPI. CS idles high through 10k. One 74AHCT125 shifts LED data to 5 V.\nPack inputs 1 (next to the hub) to 5 (lowest module): SMF4L9.0CA, LM74610-Q1 + SQ4184EY ideal diode; inputs 1-4 then pass a CSD25402Q3A\nthat is on only while no healthy pack sits below (BLKn low); otherwise the pack waits behind the FET's body diode and takes over without a gap.\nHealthy = TPS3840PL43 on the pack through 100k / 1u, 910k from VDD to its output: falls at about 4.3 V, re-arms above about 5.0 V (a swapped-in charged pack).\n22k bleeder per pack input 2-5, switched by +3V3: an empty slot floats up through the ideal diode's leakage and must not read as healthy (tools/sim_priority.py).\nUVLO, battery switch, USB switch, delay, pack divider: rev 8.1 values (TPS3840PL40, 10k / 1u, 1M, 4.7M, 2.2M / 22n, 200k / 100k), except:\nUSB detect TPS3840PL36 (a host sagging to 4.0 V at 3 A stays 'present'), 1k on the USB switch gate (break before make), 220u on SYS (tools/sim_switchover.py).\nTPS552892 makes +5V from SYS on USB and on battery (3.5 A on USB or several packs; one pack gives about 8-10 W): MODE low = PFM at light load,\n400 kHz (49.9k), FB 100k / 31.6k, EN/UVLO 100k / 54.9k (on above 3.5 V, off below 2.95 V),\nISP = ISN = VOUT (no output current limit; the ports have their own), EXTVCC and CDC open (internal VCC, no cable compensation), DITH/SYNC to GND.\nLayout (M2): AGND (pin 17) and PGND (pin 9) join only at the VCC capacitor; boot capacitors at the pins; FB and COMP away from L1 / L2.\nDNP 0R from AUX_5V to VBUS_IN: reserved for a later Qi module. Footprints still open (M2): TPS552892, CSD25483F4, inductor."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 772.16 0)
